# Telemetry Analysis Engine Conventions

## IBT Parser (`lib/ibt-parser.ts`)

- Parses iRacing `.ibt` binary telemetry files entirely in the browser.
- Returns an `IBTParsed` object with session info (YAML), channel variables, and a `readChannel()` function.
- All channel data is returned as `Float64Array` for performance.
- The session info YAML contains `CarSetup` with the complete garage setup.

## Analysis Engine (`lib/analysis-engine.ts`)

- `analyzeSession()` takes a parsed IBT, optional car profile, and track profile.
- Produces a `SessionAnalysis` result with all 14 checklist items.
- Uses car profiles for car-specific logic (brake migration, setup paths, parameter names).
- Uses track profiles for kerb zones, valid lap windows, and speed thresholds.

## Units and Conversions (`lib/unit-conversions.ts`)

Raw telemetry units differ from display units. Always convert:

| Channel | Raw | Display | Conversion |
|---------|-----|---------|------------|
| Speed | m/s | km/h | × 3.6 |
| Acceleration | m/s² | g | ÷ 9.81 |
| Pressure | kPa | PSI | ÷ 6.895 |
| Ride heights | m | mm | × 1000 |
| Shock deflections | m | mm | × 1000 |
| Steering | rad | deg | × 180/π |

## Thresholds

All analysis thresholds are defined in `lib/constants.ts`. Reference them by name:

- `TYRE_TEMP.COLD` (70°C), `TYRE_TEMP.HOT` (105°C)
- `TYRE_PRESSURE.HIGH_THRESHOLD` (24 PSI)
- `SHOCK_VELOCITY.EXTREME` (700 mm/s)
- `ANALYSIS.HIGH_SPEED_KPH` (200 km/h)
- `ENGINE_TEMP.WATER_WARNING` (110°C)

## Car Profiles (`lib/car-profiles.ts`)

Each of the five GTP cars has a profile defining:
- Setup parameter naming differences (e.g., `PushrodLengthOffset` vs `PushrodLengthDelta`)
- Brake migration availability
- Diff architecture (rear-only vs front-and-rear)
- ARB value types (descriptive vs indexed)
- Default brake bias

Car-specific JSON data lives in `src/data/car-quirks/`.

## Track Profiles (`lib/track-profiles.ts`)

Per-track profiles define:
- Kerb zones (lap distance percentages) for classifying bottoming events
- Valid lap time windows for filtering out-laps/in-laps
- Speed thresholds and setup focus areas

Track JSON data lives in `src/data/tracks/`.

## Key Rules

- Never hardcode channel names — use the `ANALYSIS_CHANNELS` array from `types.ts`.
- Always guard against missing channels (some IBT files may not contain all channels).
- Use the last 40-60% of each lap for stabilized tyre temperature readings.
- Filter laps by the track profile's `validLapWindow` to exclude out-laps and in-laps.
- Convert units at the display layer, not in the analysis engine (engine works in SI units).
